2026-09-27T09:27:26.2700003Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2700310Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2700764Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2701179Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2701312Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2701651Z ================
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2701830Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2702065Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2702587Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2702908Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2703066Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2703464Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2703706Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2703907Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2704532Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2705140Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2706204Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2707335Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2707506Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2708187Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2709084Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2709534Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2710023Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2710700Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2710858Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2795631Z ========
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2795926Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2798350Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2800505Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2800853Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2801592Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2802839Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2803758Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2804617Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2805268Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2805877Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2806033Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2806679Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2806986Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2808637Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2810464Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2811540Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2812933Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:27:26.2813254Z 
